P18-V01 full decoder declared-size parity and gate refresh — 2026-10-22 20:01 UTC

Environment: macOS AArch64, Apple M5 Max (18 logical CPUs), Rust 1.85.0.
Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`. Pinned RocketMQ Java
client/source: 5.5.1, commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

Implementation commit: `8acbf137 fix(common): ignore declared message size
while decoding`. Java `MessageDecoder.decode(ByteBuffer)` reads the store-size
field into the DTO but does not use it to bound subsequent parsing. Rust now
retains the value, parses the message fields directly, reports consumed bytes
from those fields, and applies the configured record-size limit to bytes
actually parsed. Invoked Java cases cover declared sizes zero, negative one,
and `Integer.MAX_VALUE`; a Rust regression concatenates the zero and negative
cases and checks their decoded size values and boundaries. The refreshed
`fixtures/messages/records.json` SHA-256 is
`41ed0208cdf79da2491554ed08683e4f18b40d6bce1d21d246771dd58f0e15ae`.

Fixture workflow note: a generic `exec:java` invocation selected the POM's
default `compat.Main` dispatcher and returned its usage error without writing
the fixture. Regenerated by invoking `compat.MessageDecodeFixtures` directly
with the Maven-built dependency classpath. Pinned Maven `verify` then passed.

